@[systemd-boot page]
systemd-boot is a small UEFI boot menu; it comes with systemd (after
@[enchantment install init systemd]). It is UEFI only, and it only reads the
EFI system partition (FAT): the kernel must be there. The simplest layout is
the EFI partition mounted at /boot (the disk-mount step mentions it, for
Limine; about 15 MiB per kernel, 512 MiB to 1 GiB is plenty). Not tested yet
on this ISO.

In @[enchantment chroot]:
 @[bootctl install]            # copies systemd-boot, adds a firmware entry
 @[blkid -s PARTUUID -o value /dev/sda2]   # your root partition's PARTUUID
Write /boot/loader/entries/smgl.conf (your kernel version and PARTUUID):
  title   Source Mage
  linux   /vmlinuz-6.18.59
  options root=PARTUUID=PUT-IT-HERE rw
and /boot/loader/loader.conf:
  default smgl.conf
  timeout 3
 @[bootctl list]               # checks the entry
 @[exit]

New kernels need their own entry (or edit this one). @[bootctl update]
updates systemd-boot itself after systemd is recast.
